{"type":"route","meta":{"status":200,"headers":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=3600","content-type":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8","x-robots-tag":"noindex","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/md/layout,_N_T_/md/[...slug]/layout,_N_T_/md/[...slug]/route,_N_T_/md/changelog"}},"body":"# Changelog\n\n> What has shipped in Amantrika, newest first — every entry is something you can use today, not something we plan to build.\n\n- Source: http://localhost:3000/changelog\n- Last updated: 8 August 2026\n\n---\nEverything here has shipped and is live. Anything still to come is on the\n[roadmap](/roadmap) — the two are kept apart on purpose, so a plan is never\nmistaken for a promise.\n\n## August 2026\n\n### 8 August: Showcase gallery\n\nA public [gallery](/showcase) of real invitations, shared only with their hosts'\nexplicit permission.\n\nConsent is a single unticked checkbox in the builder, and ticking it only makes\nan invitation *eligible* — we still review before anything appears. What gets\npublished is never your live invitation: it is a separate copy with the venue\naddress reduced to a city, and phone numbers, gift and payment details, and your\nentire guest list removed. First-names-only is on by default. Withdraw at any\ntime and the copy is deleted immediately, not queued for later.\n\n### 8 August: Partner programme\n\nPlanners, printers and studios can now [apply](/signup?as=agent) to build\ninvitations for their clients.\n\nEach partner gets a referral code, a dashboard covering every invitation they\nmanage, and a commission ledger that updates the moment a client pays.\nApplications are reviewed by hand — a partner cannot touch a client's\ninvitation until they are approved.\n\n### 8 August: Invitations for every occasion\n\nAmantrika is no longer wedding-only. Engagements, receptions, anniversaries,\nbirthdays, baby showers, naming ceremonies, housewarmings, graduations and\ncorporate events each get their own ceremony presets and vocabulary.\n\nThe builder reshapes itself around what you are celebrating — a birthday asks\nabout one celebrant, not two partners.\n\n### 7 August: Your own photographs\n\nUpload your own photographs instead of placeholders. They are stored securely,\ndelivered from a global CDN, and framed automatically in your theme's arch,\nscallop or polaroid style.\n\nJPG, PNG, WebP, AVIF and GIF up to 25 MB each. Uploads go straight from your\nbrowser to storage, and only you — and your partner agent, if you have one — can\nadd or remove them.\n\n### 7 August: Accounts, RSVPs and a real dashboard\n\nInvitations now live in a proper account rather than in one browser.\n\nSign in to see total views, unique visitors and a fourteen-day trend for each\ninvitation, alongside RSVPs, headcounts and meal preferences as they arrive.\nImport your whole guest list at once and copy a personalised link per guest.\n\nBlessings can be moderated before they appear, and the RSVP form and blessing\nwall can each be switched off entirely.\n\n## A note on privacy\n\nTwo decisions from this month are worth stating plainly, because they are the\nkind that are easy to get wrong quietly.\n\n### Your guests are not our data\n\nGuest names, phone numbers, RSVP messages and blessings stay in your\ninvitation's own records. They are never sent to any analytics service.\n\nWe count how many people opened an invitation using a salted hash of the\nvisitor's device that is regenerated daily — enough to tell you fifty people\nlooked rather than five, and not enough to follow anyone from one day to the\nnext.\n\n### The showcase never links to your invitation\n\nA featured invitation is always a sanitised copy at its own address. Nothing in\nthe gallery links back to a family's real invitation, and the copy carries no\nRSVP form or blessing wall — a sample must not collect anybody's details.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### How often does Amantrika change?\n\nContinuously, but this page only records changes worth your attention: new capabilities, changed behaviour, and fixes for anything that affected a live invitation. Internal refactors are not listed.\n\n### Will an update ever change my published invitation?\n\nNot its content. Your words, dates, photographs and link are yours and are never edited by us. Improvements to layout or performance apply automatically, and anything that would visibly change a published invitation is listed here.\n\n### Where can I see what is coming next?\n\nOn the roadmap. It is kept deliberately separate from this page so that nothing planned is ever mistaken for something that already works.\n"}